WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.900
When your next commission arrives, ask a bigger question:
will that relationship ever pay you again?

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.900
One sale. One person. One payment.
In a crowded red ocean, the next month starts the race again.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:27.800
Now imagine a different structure. One business. Many employees.
Renewal income for the life of the contract. A blue-ocean strategy, built around value.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:43.900
Dreams connects businesses with experts: eligible R and D and FICA tip credits,
payroll tax savings, and overpayments in taxes, premiums, and technology.
Qualifying programs can fund their costs from verified savings or recoveries.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:51.900
Now watch the math. Two professionals each create $250,000
in new first-year commissions annually, for six years.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:03.900
One gets paid once. The other adds a renewing layer every year:
$250,000, $500,000, $750,000. By year six, $1.5 million annually.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:11.900
Both stop adding new business. This illustration assumes every contract renews,
with unchanged commissions, before costs and taxes.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:23.900
Across fifty years: $1.5 million versus $71.25 million.
The difference? $69.75 million.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.500
47.5 times the total income.
Same starting production. A different structure.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:42.300
Saving from zero toward $2 million, $5 million, or $10 million over twenty years,
at an assumed 5% return, takes substantial monthly contributions.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:47.300
Renewal income can help fund your future alongside savings.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:55.000
Kongō Gumi traces its roots to 578—
1,448 years of business lineage by 2026.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Renewal income still depends on active contracts and your agreement.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.000
Build relationships. Create lasting value.
Build the income you keep.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:05.500
Dreams Business Resources.
Run your numbers at RenewalsForLife.com.
